  "bodyTypst": "Let $f$ be the function defined by $ f(x)= cases(sqrt(x + 1) & \" for \" 0 <= x <= 3, 5 - x & \" for \" 3 < x <= 5 .) $\n\n(a) Is $f$ continuous at $x = 3$ ? Explain why or why not.\n\n(b) Find the average value of $f(x)$ on the closed interval $0 <= x <= 5$.\n\n(c) Suppose the function $g$ is defined by $ g(x)= cases(k sqrt(x + 1) & \" for \" 0 <= x <= 3, m x + 2 & \" for \" 3 < x <= 5 \\,) $ where $k$ and $m$ are constants. If $g$ is differentiable at $x = 3$, what are the values of $k$ and $m$ ?",
